// A request message of the Subscribe method.
//
// Subscribes the SIM to a carrier product (a bundle) and returns the
// Bundle child it created. The SIM's Contract must be a Transatel
// Contract able to order bundles (see the Contract's account_reference,
// bundle_catalog and transatel.scopes), the product must be in the
// catalogue (see Contract ListBundleProducts) and allowed for this SIM, else
// the call fails with FAILED_PRECONDITION (INVALID_ARGUMENT for a product not
// listed).
//
// The Bundle is recorded as SUBMITTING before the order is placed.
// When the carrier confirms the order it becomes ACTIVE, or SCHEDULED for a
// future activation_time, and a later sync corrects it to the exact carrier
// status. When the carrier refuses the order or it is not sent, it becomes
// FAILED with status.error and the call fails. When the carrier's answer is
// lost, the call fails with UNAVAILABLE and the Bundle stays SUBMITTING
// until a later sync settles it: do not subscribe again with another id.
//
// The carrier has no idempotency key, so bundle_id is the key: a
// repeated request with the same bundle_id and product_id returns the
// existing Bundle, in whatever state, without a new order. The same
// bundle_id with another product_id fails with ALREADY_EXISTS.
